# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4, "Binding groups and cycles" (any line may use any name the block binds; the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else) and ch. 8 (`<-` binds the arm's plain result): the `Loud` arm gives 10, the hold above begins there, and a click adds 1.
test a_hold_above_reads_the_arms_result

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="h 10")
    1: Ui.Label(text="x")
    2: Ui.Button(label="go 10")

tick 1
  in:
    2: click
  changed:
    0: Ui.Label(text="h 11")
